patch.question:
The Gibbs energy change (in J) for the given reaction at $\ce{[Cu^{2+}]} = \ce{[Sn^{2+}]}$ = 1 M and 298 K is ___.
$\ce{Cu(s) + Sn^{2+}(aq) -> Cu^{2+}(aq) + Sn(s)}$;
$E^\circ_{\ce{Sn^{2+}/Sn}}$ = $-0.16\ \mathrm{V}$, $E^\circ_{\ce{Cu^{2+}/Cu}}$ = $0.34\ \mathrm{V}$, Take F = 96500 $\mathrm{C\,mol^{-1}}$

